##applying various filters## (this is using bcftools. this one was not used for analysis, vcf tools were used)

bcftools view -v snps -f PASS raw_variants.bcf -Ou | \
bcftools filter -e 'QUAL<30 || INFO/DP<4 || INFO/DP>200' -Ou | \
bcftools +setGT -Ou -- -t q -n . -i 'FMT/GQ<30' | \
bcftools +fill-tags -Ou -- -t MAF,F_MISSING | \
bcftools view -f PASS -i 'F_MISSING<0.7 && MAF>0.02' -Ob -o final_ddrad.bcf

##explanation of the above code##

# bcftools view -v snps -f PASS raw_variants.bcf -Ou

What it does:
-v snps → keeps only SNPs (Single Nucleotide Polymorphisms)
❌ removes indels, structural variants, etc.
-f PASS → keeps only variants that passed filters during variant calling
(FILTER column = "PASS")
-Ou → outputs uncompressed BCF to stdout
-O = output format
u = uncompressed (fast for piping)

👉 After this step:
✔ Only high-confidence SNPs remain (based on caller flags)

# bcftools filter -e 'QUAL<30 || DP<5 || DP>200 || FMT/GQ<30' -Ou
-e means:

➡️ Exclude variants where this condition is TRUE

Each condition explained:
1. QUAL<30
QUAL = variant quality score (Phred-scaled)
Removes variants with:
High probability of being false positives

✔ Threshold 30 → ~99.9% confidence

2. DP<4
DP = read depth (coverage)
Removes variants with:
Too few reads → unreliable
3. DP>200
Removes sites with excessively high coverage. Why?
Could indicate:
PCR duplicates
repetitive regions
mapping artifacts
  
ddRAD has low coverage loci → relax minimum 
Some loci get very high coverage → increase upper limit

👉 Too strict DP filtering = lose real loci
4. FMT/GQ<30
FMT/GQ = Genotype Quality (per sample)

⚠ Important:
This checks genotype confidence inside each sample
Removes variants where:
genotype calls are uncertain
  
ddRAD genotype calls are noisier
Slightly relaxing helps retain real variants

👉 After Step 2:
✔ Only variants with:
Good quality
Reasonable depth
Reliable genotype calls

bcftools view -i 'F_MISSING<0.7 && MAF>0.02' -Ob -o final_ddrad.bcf
Again, -e = exclude if condition is true

1. F_MISSING<0.7
Fraction of missing genotypes at a site
Example:
10 samples
6 missing → F_MISSING = 0.6 
F_MISSING<0.7
Why:
Missing data is expected in ddRAD
Allow up to 70% missing
👉 You can tighten later if needed

2. MAF>0.02
MAF>0.02
Why:
ddRAD datasets often have fewer loci
Keeping slightly rarer variants helps downstream analysis.
  
Why remove rare variants?
Often:
sequencing errors
low statistical power in population analysis
Output:
-Ob → compressed BCF output
-o final.bcf → saved as final file

ddRAD data typically has:
⚠️ Highly uneven coverage across loci
⚠️ Allele dropout (missing data is common)
⚠️ Stacked reads at restriction sites (can inflate DP)
  
  


  
